   2:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_exti.c ****   ******************************************************************************
   3:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_exti.c ****   * @file    stm32f4xx_exti.c
   4:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_exti.c ****   * @author  MCD Application Team
   5:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_exti.c ****   * @version V1.8.0
   6:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_exti.c ****   * @date    04-November-2016
   7:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_exti.c ****   * @brief   This file provides firmware functions to manage the following 
   8:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_exti.c ****   *          functionalities of the EXTI peripheral:
   9:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_exti.c ****   *           + Initialization and Configuration
  10:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_exti.c ****   *           + Interrupts and flags management
  11:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_exti.c ****   *
  12:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_exti.c **** @verbatim  
  13:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_exti.c **** 
  14:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_exti.c ****  ===============================================================================
  15:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_exti.c ****                               ##### EXTI features #####
  16:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_exti.c ****  ===============================================================================
  17:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_exti.c **** 
  18:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_exti.c ****  [..] External interrupt/event lines are mapped as following:
  19:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_exti.c ****    (#) All available GPIO pins are connected to the 16 external 
  20:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_exti.c ****        interrupt/event lines from EXTI0 to EXTI15.
  21:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_exti.c ****    (#) EXTI line 16 is connected to the PVD Output
  22:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_exti.c ****    (#) EXTI line 17 is connected to the RTC Alarm event
  23:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_exti.c ****    (#) EXTI line 18 is connected to the USB OTG FS Wakeup from suspend event
  24:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_exti.c ****    (#) EXTI line 19 is connected to the Ethernet Wakeup event
  25:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_exti.c ****    (#) EXTI line 20 is connected to the USB OTG HS (configured in FS) Wakeup event 
  26:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_exti.c ****    (#) EXTI line 21 is connected to the RTC Tamper and Time Stamp events
  27:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_exti.c ****    (#) EXTI line 22 is connected to the RTC Wakeup event
  28:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_exti.c ****    (#) EXTI line 23 is connected to the LPTIM Wakeup event 
  29:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_exti.c **** 
  30:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_exti.c ****                        ##### How to use this driver #####
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccjefxd3.s 			page 2


  31:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_exti.c ****  ===============================================================================
  32:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_exti.c ****  
  33:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_exti.c ****  [..] In order to use an I/O pin as an external interrupt source, follow steps 
  34:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_exti.c ****       below:
  35:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_exti.c ****    (#) Configure the I/O in input mode using GPIO_Init()
  36:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_exti.c ****    (#) Select the input source pin for the EXTI line using SYSCFG_EXTILineConfig()
  37:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_exti.c ****    (#) Select the mode(interrupt, event) and configure the trigger 
  38:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_exti.c ****        selection (Rising, falling or both) using EXTI_Init()
  39:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_exti.c ****    (#) Configure NVIC IRQ channel mapped to the EXTI line using NVIC_Init()
  40:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_exti.c **** 
  41:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_exti.c ****  [..]     
  42:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_exti.c ****    (@) SYSCFG APB clock must be enabled to get write access to SYSCFG_EXTICRx
  43:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_exti.c ****        registers using RCC_APB2PeriphClockCmd(RCC_APB2Periph_SYSCFG, ENABLE);
  44:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_exti.c **** 
  45:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_exti.c **** @endverbatim
  46:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_exti.c ****   *
  47:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_exti.c ****   ******************************************************************************
